The sources were copied rather than consumed as the published Maven artifact
(io.github.nadeemiqbal:voice-message:0.3.1) because upstream builds against
Kotlin 2.3 and this app is on Kotlin 2.0.21, which cannot read Kotlin 2.3
metadata. The code itself only uses plain AndroidX Compose APIs and compiles
unchanged here.

Modified by OrangChat: retheming onto OrangChat design tokens, Material icons in
place of upstream's hand-drawn glyphs, drag-progress state so the UI tracks the
finger, a "too short" release outcome, callbacks read through rememberUpdatedState
so they survive a channel switch, and the playback bubble dropped.

Files derived from the above: VoicePhase.kt, VoiceRecorderState.kt,
VoiceRecorderUi.kt.
